content.text:
Now heart/pendant. Current heart at (0,0.19,0.245). The bodysuit surface at y0.19 radius ~0.36*0.65=0.234, so z 0.245 is just outside. In the close-up, I don't see it; maybe hidden by the chest trim at y0.335? No, heart y0.19. The pink diamond visible at the waist is the belt gem at y0.045 z0.31. The heart may be hidden behind the bodysuit because the bodysuit is opaque and z 0.245 is only 0.011 outside; the heart scale z 0.6*0.1=0.06, so it extends to z0.305, should be visible. But it's at y0.19, which is the upper corset; maybe the chest trim or the boning hides it. Looking at the close-up, there's a pink diamond at the center around y=0.19? I see a pink diamond at the center of the corset at about y=0.05 (waist) and another at the chest? Actually the image shows a pink diamond at the center of the black corset around 720,680 (waist). The heart might be the pink diamond at 720,640? Hard to tell. Let's move the heart to y0.24, z0.31, and add a chain.

Add a pendant chain from choker (0,0.82,0.11) to heart (0,0.24,0.31):
```js
const chainMat = makeHaloMaterial(palette.halo, palette.skyAccent, 0.6);
haloMats.push(chainMat);
const chainCurve = new THREE.CatmullRomCurve3([
  new THREE.Vector3(0,0.82,0.115),
  new THREE.Vector3(0,0.62,0.2),
  new THREE.Vector3(0,0.42,0.27),
  new THREE.Vector3(0,0.28,0.305),
]);
body.add(new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.TubeGeometry(chainCurve, 24, 0.004, 6, false), chainMat));
```
But haloMats is defined after the heart section; the chain is after heart, so haloMats exists. Add after heartLight maybe. But heart position is set before. Let's edit heart position and add chain after heartLight.

Also add a chrome collar around the neck base? The choker is enough.

Eyes: add an outer iris ring in skyAccent. In the eye loop, after socket and before iris:
```js
const irisRing = new THREE.Mesh(eyeGeo, new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: palette.skyAccent, toneMapped: false }));
irisRing.position.set(side*0.102,0.043,0.255);
irisRing.scale.set(0.055,0.031,0.016);
head.add(irisRing);
```
Then the bright iris on top at z0.258 scale 0.04,0.023. The ring will be visible around the bright iris. But the eye color is near-white; the ring cyan. This gives a colored rim. Could also use palette.skyMid pink. Let's use palette.skyAccent (cyan) for a striking contrast. Add.

Reduce eye glow opacity from 0.6 to 0.4 and scale 0.2. In update, `glow.material.opacity = 0.5 + ...` overrides initial; change update to `0.3 + sin*0.12 + destruction*0.3` and scale 0.2. Currently `glow.scale.setScalar(0.3 + ...)`; change to 0.22. Let's adjust.

Also make the iris color slightly tinted? The eyeMat color is palette.eye; okay.

Add a subtle cheek blush? Could add two translucent pink spheres on cheeks, but may look muddy. Skip.

Neck: widen the neck cylinder bottom to 0.14 and add a chrome collar ring at y0.72 radius 0.14. Maybe not needed.

Let's edit heart and chain.

